    "knowledge_point": {
      "db_id": 17592186133831,
      "id": "e34a2cbf-0bed-50eb-9e62-7c6e55560cb9",
      "title": "Constructing Line Integrals of a Vector-Valued Functions Over Plane Curves"
    },
    "question": {
      ":question/id": "caece77c-48bb-5511-a033-0a5ace591e24",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/problem": "Which ordinary definite integral represents $\\int_C \\mathbf{F}\\cdot\\mathrm{d}\\mathbf{r}$ given that $\\mathbf{F}(x,y)=(- x)\\,\\mathbf{i}+(- y + 2)\\,\\mathbf{j}$ and $C$ is the path $\\mathbf{r}(t)=(\\sin{\\left(t \\right)})\\,\\mathbf{i}+(\\cos{\\left(t \\right)})\\,\\mathbf{j}$ for $t\\in [0,2]$?\n\nUse the supplied parameterization and limits. Select the integral whose integrand is $\\mathbf{F}(\\mathbf{r}(t))\\cdot \\mathbf{r}^{\\prime}(t)$; do not evaluate it.\n\n*Hint: $\\mathbf{r}^{\\prime}(t)=(\\cos{\\left(t \\right)})\\,\\mathbf{i}+(- \\sin{\\left(t \\right)})\\,\\mathbf{j}$. Substitute both coordinates into the field, then take the dot product.*",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Use the vector line-integral formula:\n\n$$\n\\int_C \\mathbf{F}\\cdot\\mathrm{d}\\mathbf{r}=\\int_a^b \\mathbf{F}(\\mathbf{r}(t))\\cdot \\mathbf{r}^{\\prime}(t)\\,\\mathrm{d}t.\n$$\n\nSubstitute the coordinates $x=\\sin{\\left(t \\right)}$ and $y=\\cos{\\left(t \\right)}$ into both field components:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf{F}(\\mathbf{r}(t))&=(- (\\sin{\\left(t \\right)}))\\,\\mathbf{i}\\\\&\\quad+(- (\\cos{\\left(t \\right)}) + 2)\\,\\mathbf{j}\\\\&=(- \\sin{\\left(t \\right)})\\,\\mathbf{i}\\\\&\\quad+(- \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} + 2)\\,\\mathbf{j}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDifferentiate each path component:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x^{\\prime}(t)&=\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}(\\sin{\\left(t \\right)})=\\cos{\\left(t \\right)},\\\\y^{\\prime}(t)&=\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}(\\cos{\\left(t \\right)})=- \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiply matching components and add:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\mathbf{F}(\\mathbf{r}(t))\\cdot \\mathbf{r}^{\\prime}(t)\\\\&=(- \\sin{\\left(t \\right)})(\\cos{\\left(t \\right)})\\\\&\\quad+(- \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} + 2)(- \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSimplify the products using $\\sin^2 t+\\cos^2 t=1$ where applicable:\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{F}(\\mathbf{r}(t))\\cdot \\mathbf{r}^{\\prime}(t)=- 2 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}.\n$$\n\nKeep the supplied parameter limits. The required integral is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\int_{0}^{2}\\bigl[(- \\sin{\\left(t \\right)})(\\cos{\\left(t \\right)})\\\\&\\quad+(- \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} + 2)(- \\sin{\\left(t \\right)})\\bigr]\\,\\mathrm{d}t\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "03ef84f3-c7c6-59d8-a9b7-8c8b1faa14e0",
          ":answer-field/key": "selection",
          ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/radio",
          ":answer-field/choices": [
            {
              ":answer/id": "c8a365ff-a56e-5a63-9fba-b0fc0c4abfd2",
